  "name": "The Aleutian Islands: America's Back Door",
  "description": "This book is about the Aleutian Islands, Alaska. The author, Isobel W. Hutchison, took a journey through the Aleutian Islands and Alaska, in the mid 1930's reporting about the history of the Islands and beginning of a defense system with the Coast Guard against Japan. Along the way, she encounters natives of the islands. [Reference: Hutchison, IW. 1937. The Aleutian Islands: American's Back Door. Blackie & Son Limited.] This volume may be found at many university libraries.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To show the history of the Aleutian Islands (America's back door)",
